  {
    "name": "the broker check allows for what the broker holds against an account for rows not yet final",
    "spec": "SPEC.md, the header: the broker check, what a broker holds against an account",
    "working": [
      "Rule (SPEC.md header, the broker check): compare the book's cash less the holds as they stood when the broker stated its cash (cash_read) with that cash; the sentence gives the book's figure net of the holds. A limit buy holds its stated amount; a put sold without margin holds strike x multiplier x contracts opened beyond the account's longs, less the stated premium; in a margin account a put sale holds no cash; a buy with no stated amount or a withdrawal holds an unstated amount, so its currency's check waits (pending).",
      "L (TFSA): book USD 1000 (l1). Hold: buy stating 70, read as a limit buy working in full -> 70. Net 1000 - 70 = 930 = broker 930. No difference.",
      "M (cash): book USD 1000 (m1). Hold: buy with no stated amount -> unstated, USD check waits. Net of known holds 1000 vs broker 900: differs, pending. own 1000.00 (no hold amount known to net), broker 900.00. differences 1, pending 1.",
      "P (TFSA, no margin): book USD 2000 (p1). Hold: put sale of 1 W; P holds no long W, so 1 contract opened beyond longs: 10 x 100 x 1 - 50 = 950. Net 2000 - 950 = 1050 = broker 1050. No difference.",
      "Q (margin): book USD 2000 (q1). The put sale is secured by buying power, not cash: hold 0. Net 2000 = broker 2000. No difference.",
      "R (TFSA): book USD 2000 - 100 = 1900 (r1, r2), holding 1 long Y. Hold: put sale of 1 Y; contracts opened beyond the 1 long Y held = 0, so nothing is cash-secured: hold 0 (READING: the literal formula 10 x 100 x 0 - 80 = -80 would be a negative hold; a hold is never negative, and a sale against a long held opens nothing). Net 1900 = broker 1900. No difference.",
      "S (TFSA): book USD 1000 - 500 = 500 and 10 X (s1, s2). No holds. Cash 500 = broker 500; units 10 X = broker 10 X as of 2026-01-07. No difference.",
      "T (cash): book CAD 1000 (t1). Hold: buy stating 100 -> 100. Net 1000 - 100 = 900 vs broker 850: differs, said. own 900.00, broker 850.00. differences 1, pending 0.",
      "U (cash): book CAD 1000 (u1). Hold: withdrawal, amount unstated -> CAD check waits. 1000 vs broker 600: differs, pending. own 1000.00, broker 600.00. differences 1, pending 1.",
      "V: cash 3,000 − 100 (one long W bought) = 2,900 USD; the working sale of 3 W contracts closes the 1 long and opens 2: hold = (3,000 collateral − 150 premium) × 2/3 = 1,900 (SPEC: the premium's share, by contracts, of those it opens); book net 2,900 − 1,900 = 1,000.00 against the broker's 1,100.00: one difference, said."
    ],
